  {
   "id": 35,
   "type": "Note",
   "pos": [
    60,
    -420
   ],
   "size": [
    500,
    380
   ],
   "flags": {},
   "order": 0,
   "mode": 0,
   "inputs": [],
   "outputs": [],
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "FAST DE-ROPE (H3 fast-motion smear fix)\n\nRequires matlowai/ComfyUI-MAINodes (Jerk Oracle, Time Smear, V2V Init, Inject Schedule, Exact Recover), taeh3.safetensors (madebyollin/taehv, encoder+decoder) in models/vae_approx, an H3 turbo LoRA for pass 2, and OpenCV for the Motion Gate. Use the fp16 video VAE for the final decode if you don't have the int8 one.\n1. PASS 1 is your normal render; its audio is the soundtrack.\n2. MOTION GATE measures pass 1 (optical flow, camera pans and shot cuts excluded) and keeps only sustained EXTREME motion. Calm clips (dialogue, gentle motion) skip pass 2 entirely: SEGMENT SPLICE never asks for it.\n3. The burst (+12-frame handles) is slowed down with MAINodes' Time Smear and redrawn in PASS 2 with H3 WINDOW ATTENTION: each frame attends exactly to nearby frames, anchors and all text/audio rows, ~40% cheaper than full attention on the 2-3x longer slowed clip, fast poses as crisp or crisper.\n4. taeh3 does the throwaway decode/encode; Exact Recover returns to real time; Segment Splice crossfades the burst back into the full-quality pass 1.\n15 s at 1 MP: set d_max 3 (Motion Gate + Time Smear) if pass 2 runs out of memory."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 36,
   "type": "Note",
   "pos": [
    580,
    -420
   ],
   "size": [
    500,
    380
   ],
   "flags": {},
   "order": 0,
   "mode": 0,
   "inputs": [],
   "outputs": [],
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "DRAWING DE-ROPE (2s)\n\nInside the gated burst, anime only needs a new drawing every 2 frames, so only those drawings are slowed down and redrawn: each gets one static latent token, aligned to H3's token grid (key poses such as impacts get two, so pass 2 commits to them; shot cuts always start a new drawing). Drawing Recover holds each redrawn drawing over its 2-frame slot: the burst comes back crisp and already on 2s. Pass 2 was 8-26% cheaper than the per-frame fast de-rope in our tests (more on long bursts), same crispness, impacts on the same frames."
   ]
  }
